---
title: Anatidae
---
# Anatidae

Anatidae is the duck, goose and swan family, some hundred and seventy species of
webbed-footed waterbirds found on every continent but Antarctica. Feeding ranges
from grazing on land through dabbling at the surface to descending for
invertebrates on the bottom. Most species moult all their flight feathers at once
and are flightless for a few weeks each year. See [[mallard]] and [[mute-swan]].
